      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for reviewing the patch and for bringing up this great point!\n\nFrom the BMC firmware implementation perspective, we currently rely on the MCTP response payload from the SMA device, which explicitly tells us the number of available sensors. We instantiate the DBus objects based on this payload to prevent unnecessary polling and false-positive faults on empty ports.\n\nHowever, regarding how the device handles a situation where a sensor should be present but is disconnected or faulty, we are not fully aware of the internal hardware detection mechanisms.\n\n@haghera@nvidia.com Would you kindly help explain the hardware behavior in this scenario? Specifically, how does the SMA device detect this, and what would it return to the BMC via MCTP if an expected sensor is faulty or unconnected?",
